# Chat Rendering — Sustainability & Robustness Plan

**Status**: Proposal
**Owner**: TBD
**Date**: 2026-05-02
**Goal**: Make the agent chat history render pipeline world-class — robust under high-volume streaming, sustainable to evolve, and free of the layout/jank/format bugs that surface today.

---

## 1. Goals & Non-Goals

### Goals
- Zero layout jank during streaming (no scroll jumps, no item overlap, no flicker).
- One render per animation frame max during streaming, regardless of token rate.
- Bounded memory and CPU on long sessions (≥10k timeline items, hours-long streams).
- Per-message-type rendering is isolated, memoized, and independently testable.
- Tool output rendering survives malformed / partial / oversized payloads gracefully.
- HTML in agent output is rendered safely (no XSS, no broken-DOM).
- All scroll/follow behavior owned by a single subsystem — no fighting libraries.
- Replayable golden fixtures for streaming sessions; regressions are caught in CI.

### Non-Goals
- Redesigning the chat *event protocol* (`AgentEvent`) — we keep the existing wire format.
- Replacing the reducer with global state (Redux/Zustand) — the reducer model fits.
- Changing tool semantics or what tools exist.
- Rewriting the composer / autocomplete / loop-mode UX.

