## 4. Migration Plan (phases)

Each phase ships independently, behind a feature flag (`chat.renderV2`) where useful, and lands on `main` without breaking existing behavior.

### Phase 0 — Repro harness & baselines (≤1 day)
- Capture 3 real streaming sessions to JSONL fixtures (short, medium, tool-heavy).
- Build `<ChatPanelHarness>` dev page that replays a fixture at configurable rate.
- Add `pnpm test:chat:perf` — measures: renders/sec, longest frame, scroll-jump count, parse time. Records baseline numbers.
- **Exit criteria**: We can reproduce the screenshot bug class deterministically.

### Phase 1 — Cheap wins (≤2 days, no architecture change)
- Wrap each renderer in `renderers.tsx` with `React.memo` keyed on item identity.
- Memoize `GhMarkdown` body on text content; cache markdown AST in a small LRU keyed by `(messageId, blockIndex)`.
- Per-kind `estimateSize` map: `{ user: 80, text: 120, thinking: 100, tool: 280, result: 60, ... }`.
- Memoize `LinkifiedText` regex output per `text` value.
- Strip ANSI escapes at the renderer boundary (single util, well-tested).
- Sanitize markdown via `rehype-sanitize` with a tight allowlist (drop `rehype-raw`, or run it then sanitize).
- Add `'-uno'`-style guards for malformed `rawContent` shapes.
- **Exit criteria**: Baseline perf numbers improve ≥40% without touching virt/scroll stack.

### Phase 2 — View-layer rewrite (≤3 days)
- Extract `<ChatTimeline>` from ChatPanel — owns Virtuoso, follow-output, anchoring, search-jump.
- Remove `useStickToBottom`. Virtuoso owns scroll.
- Remove `useVirtualizer`. Virtuoso replaces it.
- Remove all nested `max-h-64` scrollers; replace with "Show all" expand.
- Behind `chat.renderV2` flag — both implementations available, default off, enable for self-dogfood for a week.
- **Exit criteria**: Replay harness shows zero scroll jumps and zero item overlap on tool-heavy fixture.

### Phase 3 — Stream batching (≤1 day)
- In `useChatSession`, queue events arriving within a frame; flush on `requestAnimationFrame`.
- Coalesce `stream-block-delta` of the same `(messageId, blockIndex)` — concatenate text deltas, keep last partial JSON.
- Reducer receives batched updates; at most one dispatch per frame.
- **Exit criteria**: At 200 tokens/sec input rate, React renders ≤ 60/sec on the chat surface.

### Phase 4 — Reducer hardening (≤2 days)
- Adopt Immer in `chatTimelineReducer`. Replace `state.timeline.slice(); t[i] = next; return …` with `produce(state, draft => { draft.timeline[i].text += event.text })`.
- Add `rev: number` to every TimelineItem; bump on mutation.
- Memo equality in renderers becomes `(prev.item.id === next.item.id && prev.item.rev === next.item.rev)`.
- Tool partial-JSON: introduce `parsePartialJson()` — best-effort parse, returns `{ keys: string[]; preview: Record<string, unknown> | null }`. Renderers use this for skeleton UI.
- **Exit criteria**: Tool cards never blank during streaming. Reducer perf within 10% of pre-Immer baseline.

### Phase 5 — Component split & API freeze (≤2 days)
- Split ChatPanel into:
  - `<ChatPanel>` — orchestrator (≤200 LOC)
  - `<ChatHeader>` — mode pill, override notice, search bar, loop banner
  - `<ChatTimeline>` — scroll + virt + render (Phase 2 output)
  - `<ChatComposer>` — textarea, autocomplete, send, attachments
  - `<ChatContextProvider>` — replaces deep prop drilling for actions/session
- Public types frozen: `TimelineItem` discriminated union is the contract between layers.
- **Exit criteria**: ChatPanel ≤200 LOC. Each child unit-testable in isolation.

### Phase 6 — Observability & guardrails (≤1 day)
- Dev-only render counter overlay (toggle via setting): items rendered, frames/sec, longest frame.
- `pnpm test:chat:perf` wired into CI, fails build if perf regresses >15% vs baseline.
- Golden fixture diff test: replay each fixture, snapshot final DOM, fail on diff.
- **Exit criteria**: Regression in any of the above blocks merge.

### Phase 7 — Flag flip & cleanup (≤1 day)
- Default `chat.renderV2` ON. Remove old code paths.
- Remove `useStickToBottom` dep.
- Remove `tanstack-virtual` dep (if no other consumer).
- Schedule cleanup agent to remove the flag in 2 weeks.

**Total**: ~12 working days, shippable in increments. Phase 1 alone fixes the loudest issues.

