## 5. Verification Strategy

### 5.1 Replay fixtures (the single most important asset)
Stored at `packages/domains/terminal/src/client/__fixtures__/chat-streams/`. Each fixture is a JSONL of `AgentEvent` records captured from a real session. Categories:
- `short-text.jsonl` — single short assistant turn
- `long-text.jsonl` — long streamed assistant turn
- `tool-heavy.jsonl` — many tool calls with partial JSON
- `mixed.jsonl` — full session with thinking, text, tools, results
- `malformed.jsonl` — truncated / corrupted events to test resilience

The harness can replay at any rate (real-time, 10×, 100×, instant).

### 5.2 Performance budgets (CI-enforced)
| Metric | Budget |
|---|---|
| Longest frame during streaming | ≤ 16ms (p99) |
| Renders per second on chat surface during streaming | ≤ 60 |
| Scroll-jump count during a tool-heavy fixture | 0 |
| Markdown parse time per delta | ≤ 1ms (incremental cache hit) |
| Memory growth over 10k items | ≤ linear, no leaks |

### 5.3 Visual regression
- Snapshot key DOM states (first paint, mid-stream, post-stream, after expand) per fixture.
- Diff in CI; visual diffs require explicit approval.

### 5.4 E2E (Playwright)
- One streaming-chat e2e test: send a prompt, replay a fixture into the renderer, assert no `data-jank-detected` attribute appears.

